[[File:Felanitx Portocolom 03 ies.jpg|thumb|The video for "You're Beautiful" was filmed at Sa Cova Foradada in Portocolom.]]
The music video for "You're Beautiful" was filmed on 23 March 2005<ref>{{Cite web |date=2006 |title=James Blunt - You're Beautiful (Making Of) |url=https://archive.org/details/youre-beautiful-making-of |website=Internet Archive}}</ref> at Sa Cova Foradada in [[Felanitx|Portocolom]], [[Mallorca]]. It was directed by Sam Brown and [[Robbie Ryan (cinematographer)|Robbie Ryan]], with Flynn Productions. Blunt removes the upper portion of his clothing in a cold, bare, snowy setting with the sea behind him and places all of his personal belongings on the ground. While doing this, [[seagulls]] circle overhead like [[buzzards]].<ref>{{cite web|title=ManchesterOnline.co.uk |work=Watch James Blunt's "You're Beautiful" video – what it's about |url=http://www.manchesteronline.co.uk/entertainment/music/audioandvideo/s/159/159996_watch_james_blunts_youre_beautiful_video.html |access-date=11 March 2006 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20060305151754/http://www.manchesteronline.co.uk/entertainment/music/audioandvideo/s/159/159996_watch_james_blunts_youre_beautiful_video.html |archive-date=5 March 2006 |url-status=dead }}</ref> At the end of the video, he jumps off a cliff into the water while he sings the lyrics: "But it's time to face the truth, I will never be with you". According to Blunt, he had to jump twice and suffered a split lip in the jumps.

At least one writer's interpretation is that it shows Blunt [[suicide|taking his own life]], perhaps following a Japanese tradition of removing one's shoes and contents of clothing prior to jumping from a great height.<ref>{{cite web|last=Gordenker |first=Alice |url=http://search.japantimes.co.jp/cgi-bin/ek20060117wh.html |title=Suicide &#124; The Japan Times |publisher=Search.japantimes.co.jp |date=17 January 2006 |access-date=2 April 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite web| title=BlogCritics.org| work=Keep an Eye on James Blunt| url=http://blogcritics.org/keep-an-eye-on-james-blunt/| access-date=11 March 2006| archive-date=11 January 2016| archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160111141843/http://blogcritics.org/keep-an-eye-on-james-blunt/| url-status=dead}}</ref> However, the director of the video states in a "making-of" piece of footage that "the idea [of the video] is built around the last line, where he says, 'I'll never be with you', and that idea of completely forgetting about something, of getting rid of that emotion, and moving on, and I think that the video is a sort of visual manifestation of that emotion."<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CVJQVt2pawU |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/varchive/youtube/20211213/CVJQVt2pawU |archive-date=13 December 2021 |url-status=live|title=James Blunt - You're Beautiful (Making Of)|last=James Blunt|date=17 May 2007|via=YouTube}}{{cbignore}}</ref>

On 9 November 2021, Blunt announced a 4K remaster of the video on his Instagram.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.instagram.com/p/CWEIrVlItj9/ |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/iarchive/s/instagram/CWEIrVlItj9 |archive-date=26 December 2021 |url-access=registration|title=James Blunt on Instagram: YOU'RE BEAUTIFUL Now in 4K}}{{cbignore}}</ref>{{sup|{{note|a|[a]}}}}

The video has been parodied in a ''[[Dead Ringers (series)|Dead Ringers]]'' spoof, with [[Jon Culshaw]] impersonating Blunt, singing the song with different lyrics where he explains how he can be cool.{{Citation needed|date=January 2020}}

sections.text:
thumb|The video for "You're Beautiful" was filmed at Sa Cova Foradada in Portocolom.
The music video for "You're Beautiful" was filmed on 23 March 2005 at Sa Cova Foradada in Portocolom, Mallorca. It was directed by Sam Brown and Robbie Ryan, with Flynn Productions. Blunt removes the upper portion of his clothing in a cold, bare, snowy setting with the sea behind him and places all of his personal belongings on the ground. While doing this, seagulls circle overhead like buzzards. At the end of the video, he jumps off a cliff into the water while he sings the lyrics: "But it's time to face the truth, I will never be with you". According to Blunt, he had to jump twice and suffered a split lip in the jumps.

At least one writer's interpretation is that it shows Blunt taking his own life, perhaps following a Japanese tradition of removing one's shoes and contents of clothing prior to jumping from a great height. However, the director of the video states in a "making-of" piece of footage that "the idea [of the video] is built around the last line, where he says, 'I'll never be with you', and that idea of completely forgetting about something, of getting rid of that emotion, and moving on, and I think that the video is a sort of visual manifestation of that emotion."

On 9 November 2021, Blunt announced a 4K remaster of the video on his Instagram.{{sup|{{note|a|[a]}}}}

The video has been parodied in a Dead Ringers spoof, with Jon Culshaw impersonating Blunt, singing the song with different lyrics where he explains how he can be cool.{{Citation needed|date=January 2020}}

